    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nPlugins or user scripts that want to define per-client behavior have to maintain their own data and lifecycle.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAdd a user_data field to the `vim.lsp.Client` class so custom data can be written there without triggering diagnostics.\n\nI can submit a PR for this if it's the right direction. If not, can be disregarded/closed.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "A `.data` field is probably fine. Internally we add `_foo` fields to the client object as needed, and I think some lsp configs do so as well. Presumably the configs should be migrated.",
